id: training-support
name: Training Support
kind: crafting
categories: weights
slots: 2
prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in the Concealment Skill
source: Core Rule
description: >
  While Holding Back, the Weights take nothing off your Combat Rolls. Needs 2+ Ranks in
  Concealment in whoever wears it.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: If you possess any stacks of Holding Back while wearing this Apparel, you may
  ignore the reduction to your Combat Rolls from the effects of the Weight Apparel Category.
text: >
  Training Support: This outfit is heavy, but doesn’t restrict your movement.
  –Apparel Category: Weights
  –Prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in the Concealment Skill
  –Quality Slots: 2
  –Effects: If you possess any stacks of Holding Back while wearing this Apparel, you may ignore
  the reduction to your Combat Rolls from the effects of the Weight Apparel Category.

---

# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Weights Category's reduction comes with the rest of the Apparel rules. It asks
# weightsPenaltyWaived() in module/gear.mjs whether to leave it off: this Quality on the piece,
# a wearer with 2+ Ranks in Concealment, and any stacks of Holding Back. "You may" is taken as
# always - nobody chooses a penalty.

[passive]
if (concealment.ranks >= 2) {
  piece.waivesWeightsWhileHoldingBack = true;
}
